All gallery Chinese strings are enumerable — titles/summaries come from SceneCatalog at runtime; menu literals are the two Program strings; MaterialBinding labels — check that file quickly (grep showed no Chinese labels beyond what's listed? MaterialBinding labels use `{_blendModes[i]}` — blend mode names probably English enums). The collected set: scene titles/summaries (runtime via SceneCatalog) + 2 menu strings + a safety buffer.

Rewrite BuildCodepoints:
```csharp
private static List<int> BuildCodepoints()
{
    var used = new HashSet<int>();
    for (int c = 32; c < 127; c++) used.Add(c);
    used.Add('—'); used.Add('·'); // 标点兜底
    void collect(string? s) { if (s != null) foreach (char ch in s) used.Add(ch); }
    collect("Ludots Engine Gallery — raylib 引擎渲染能力 18 项");
    collect("数字/字母选择场景，Enter 启动，ESC 退出；场景内 ESC 返回菜单，R 复位相机");
    collect("[ESC] menu   [R] reset camera");
    foreach (var d in SceneCatalog.Descriptors) { collect(d.Title); collect(d.Summary); }
    return used.OrderBy(c => c).ToList();
}
```
This gives ~600 glyphs → tiny atlas, no crash. Plus unhandled chars → box glyph (visual only, no crash).

Also add "：" "，" "；" are inside the collected strings automatically ✓. Bulletproof enough. Remove unused FindSystemCjkFont? Keep. Rewrite GalleryFont accordingly, rebuild, kill any leftover process, relaunch.

