```csharp
public sealed unsafe class RaylibLitModel : IDisposable
{
    private Shader _shader;
    private RaylibFrameLightingLocations _lightingLocs;  // reuse resolve (uniform set matches instancing + mine)
    private int _locRoughness, _locMetallic, _locSkyZenith, _locSkyGround;
    private int _locShadowMap, _locLightSpace, _locShadowEnabled, _locShadowTexelWorld;
    private RaylibDirectionalShadowMap? _shadow;
    private RaylibFrameLighting? _lighting;
    private Vector3 _viewPos;

    ctor(): load model_lit shader; resolve locations fail-loud (incl. shadow uniforms).

    SetLighting(RaylibFrameLighting lighting, Vector3 viewPos)  // per frame before draws
    SetShadow(RaylibDirectionalShadowMap? shadow, float texelWorld)
    DrawMesh(Mesh, RaylibMatrix transform, Vector4 tint, float roughness, float metallic)  // per draw: set uniforms + DrawMesh
    AttachToModel(Model model)  // set all materials' shader = _shader (then DrawModelEx uses it; uniforms persist per draw via SetShaderValue before DrawModelEx)
    Dispose
}
```
Note DrawModelEx with custom-shader material: raylib's DrawModelEx sets mvp/model + colDiffuse (material color) + texture0 (albedo map) automatically ✓ (like DrawMesh). tint uniform is ours (set per draw). colDiffuse comes from material.maps[ALBEDO].color? raylib sets colDiffuse = material color — for props we pass tint via our uniform and keep colDiffuse white.

Shared props helper `RaylibLitProps`: GenMeshCube/Sphere cached + DrawCube/DrawSphere wrappers over RaylibLitModel.

